     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""Does one unsupported Step 2 revision relation change what the frozen judge reads? An offline replay of the saved D392 clean draw 1.
     3	
     4	No request leaves this process: every judge request is answered from the saved judging archive of the draw
     5	(`poc/data/clean-e2e-2026-11-09/stage2-clean-d1/judged/archive.sqlite`) by `control_v108.ReferenceArchiveTransport`, which answers
     6	only a byte-identical canonical request and raises on any other. The credential reader and the production transport are replaced by a
     7	refusal while a replay runs.
     8	
     9	  edge_replay.py control <new folder>
    10	      The untouched draw through the current adapter and the frozen judge. Passes only when every request finds its saved answer,
    11	      every saved row is used, and the ledger, the judge requests and the answers equal the saved run's.
    12	  edge_replay.py counterfactual <new folder> <control folder> --by 70:e4 --revised-group 69:e5 [--keep-links]
    13	      The same replay over a copy of the library with exactly that one revision relation removed (the copy carries its own stamp; the
    14	      saved library is not touched). It stops at the first judging round whose requests differ from the control's (a request with other
    15	      text, a request the control did not send, or a control request not sent) and writes the requests of that round, both versions.
    16	      Nothing after that round is replayed: later state would rest on answers to requests the archive does not hold.
    17	      --keep-links removes the relation but writes the links the new record inherited through it, to separate the inherited link from
    18	      the relation itself.
    19	
    20	What a replay shows: whether, and in which round, the judge's input changes. What it cannot show: any answer to a changed request."""
