   179	def check_schema(value, schema, path='$', root=None):
   180	    """A small validator for the subset of JSON Schema the prompts use: object/required/additionalProperties,
   181	    array/items/minItems, string/enum/pattern, integer, number, boolean, null in anyOf, and $ref into the root's $defs."""
   182	    root = root if root is not None else schema
   183	    if '$ref' in schema:
   184	        name = schema['$ref'].rsplit('/', 1)[1]
   185	        schema = root['$defs'][name]
   186	    kind = schema.get('type')
   187	    if 'anyOf' in schema:
   188	        # a value matching no option reports the closest options' errors (fewest), not merely the last option's
   189	        failures = []
   190	        for option in schema['anyOf']:
   191	            errors = check_schema(value, option, path, root)
   192	            if not errors:
   193	                return []
   194	            failures.append(errors)
   195	        fewest = min((len(errors) for errors in failures), default=0)
   408	## 9. Workspace and operations
   409	
   410	- Inspect a path before writing to it; new stored data gets a new, dated name; chain guarded steps with `&&`. Deleting stored data needs
   411	  Alex's request, a backup, exactly identified items and a log entry.
   412	- Absolute paths. Commands run under zsh: pass a list as an array. No foreground `sleep`.
   413	- Preserve existing and concurrent changes: never reset, clean or stash work that is not yours. Never run parallel agents that edit
   414	  shared modules.
   415	- When Alex names a step, the test is that step alone through its own harness (extraction: stored requests re-sent, answers sifted,
   416	  scored against the gold). A full-pipeline run, a registered test, or a paid send beyond the probes of a few cents an agreed direction
   417	  allows (§7.3) starts only on his explicit word (Alex, 2026-10-27: "我不是要你看下step 1抽取到底行不行？").
   418	- A long paid run is launched detached in a new session with a log and pid file, after checking machine and network health; nothing heavy
   419	  runs beside paid calls. A gate runs on a snapshot no one is editing.
   420	- Never open a live run's databases: run `sh <run folder>/snapshot.sh` and query the snapshot.
   421	- No edit to package code or prompt files while any run is live: the parallel day's manifest hashes every `.py` and prompt file and
   422	  fails the day. Edit in another worktree or wait.
   423	- Experiment harnesses send concurrently (a thread pool of 8; the archive is thread-safe); serial sends waste the wall clock Alex is
   424	  waiting on.
   425	- **Run settings** (`scripts/replay.py`): extraction requests prepared 16 at a time (`--workers`; the measurement launcher passes its
   426	  `HIVEMIND_WORKERS` there), Jev matching 8 at a time (`--jev-workers`), judgements 32 at a time (`judging.JUDGE_WORKERS`); a model call
   427	  times out after 180 s and is tried up to three times.
   428	  The three draws of a measurement run at once, one launcher each (`docs/research/2026-11-01-e2e-loop/harness/run_arm.sh`). Measured
   429	  timings: `docs/poc/pipeline-plan.md`, "Run settings and timing".
   430	- Report results as they land; scope delegated work so a first useful result returns within 20–30 minutes.
   431	- Services for testing run on the host (README, "Run the service for testing"): on this Mac the VPN gives Docker containers no outbound
   432	  internet, so a model or embedding call fails inside Docker. Start them with a log and pid file, check them with
   433	  `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8788/days`, and stop what you started before handing over. Changing Docker or VPN networking is Alex's call.
   434	- Credentials never appear in Git, documents, logs, prompts, stored data, URLs or command arguments; they are kept in the owner-only file
   435	  `~/.config/hivemind/credentials.json`, outside the repository. Never raise a spending cap, and never switch a provider or model
   436	  silently.
